// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_own_flat.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: `layer()`'s third P3-Task-9 guard (engine/level/scene_dsl.emp) — a
// `deform: Own(..)` whose two amplitude shifts are BOTH 15, i.e. a per-layer table the
// layer never samples.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "attaches a table this layer never samples"
//
// THIS GUARD IS LOAD-BEARING TWICE, which is why it gets its own case rather than being
// filed as authoring hygiene:
//
//   1. IT IS WHAT MAKES `CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE ⇒ CAP_DEFORM` STRUCTURAL. `scene_caps()`
//      pins that implication, and the pin is only ever satisfiable because an own() layer
//      is guaranteed to contribute a live amplitude. The RUNTIME depends on it: the
//      per-band table reload is emitted INSIDE the `cap_deform_sample` block in
//      Parallax_Fill_PerLine, because a5/a6 are the sampling machinery's registers and
//      nothing else reads them. A mask with $0020 and not $0004 would elide the enclosing
//      block and leave the bit selecting a site that is not there.
//   2. THE FLAT-PATHED IDIOM ALREADY HAS A CORRECT SPELLING ONE LEVEL UP. Attaching a
//      zero table at shift 15 purely to force the per-line pipeline is what OJZ's shipped
//      configs do — at SCENE level, where it costs one header word. At LAYER level the
//      same trick costs a band_ext extension in EVERY band of the game plus a per-band
//      pointer reload in the fill loop, and buys nothing `precision: PRECISION_LINE` does
//      not buy for free.
//
// THE TWO-FIXTURE DIFFERENTIAL. The contrast is ONE PAYLOAD SLOT — own()'s shift_b:
//
//   FIXTURE A — `Own(0, 15, 2, 0, 1)`: shift_b live. Legal; folds to $0025 =
//               CAP_PER_LINE | CAP_DEFORM | CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE. Its ensure MUST STAY
//               GREEN, and it is also the only place in the poison set that asserts the
//               positive form of the implication scene_caps() pins.
//   FIXTURE B — `Own(0, 15, 15, 0, 1)`: both shifts at the no-deform sentinel. One
//               diagnostic, from layer()'s guard.
//
// EXPECTED COUNT 2, AND THE PAIR IS THE ASSERTION — the same shape as the R1 Task 9
// band() minima cases, arrived at the same way. `ensure` is non-aborting, so layer()
// refuses the flat own() and constructs the layer anyway (both shifts 15); scene_caps()
// then folds it to $0021 and the CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE ⇒ CAP_DEFORM pin fires in its own
// words, because the amplitude that would have supplied $0004 is precisely the one the
// constructor just refused. $0020 is raised by the VARIANT and $0004 by the AMPLITUDE:
// separating them is what this guard is for, and the second diagnostic is that separation
// being observed rather than asserted.
//
// (This was PREDICTED as count 1 when the case was written and MEASURED as 2. The
// prediction is recorded rather than quietly corrected: it was wrong because it assumed
// the fold would still see a live amplitude from somewhere, and the whole point of the
// guard is that with a flat own() there is nowhere for one to come from.)
//
// A DROP TO 1 MEANS ONE OF THE TWO STOPPED FIRING, and which one matters. The
// constructor's guard is what keeps the RUNTIME honest — the per-band table reload is
// emitted inside the `cap_deform_sample` block, so a mask with $0020 and not $0004 selects
// a site that is not there. The fold's pin is the backstop that keeps the implication from
// being a claim in a comment. The lane's expected fragment names the constructor's, so a 1
// that kept only the fold's would fail on the fragment too.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_own_flat

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// FIXTURE A — a per-layer table the layer actually samples.
const POISON_OWNFLAT_SCENE_A: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2,
                    deform: SceneDeform.Own(0, 15, 2, 0, 1)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 3,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 1))

// FIXTURE B — the same, with own()'s shift_b at the no-deform sentinel.
const POISON_OWNFLAT_SCENE_B: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2,
                    deform: SceneDeform.Own(0, 15, 15, 0, 1)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 3,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 1))

// Fixture A's capabilities, derived by hand: a table is attached (both scene-level and
// per-layer), so CAP_PER_LINE $0001; own()'s shift_b is live, so CAP_DEFORM $0004; the
// layer carries its own table, so CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE $0020. No column table, no
// anchor, one-element registry.
const POISON_OWNFLAT_DECLARED = $0025
const POISON_OWNFLAT_FOLDED_A = fold_caps([POISON_OWNFLAT_SCENE_A])
const POISON_OWNFLAT_FOLDED_B = fold_caps([POISON_OWNFLAT_SCENE_B])

// ---- FIXTURE A, THE PASSING HALF ----
ensure(POISON_OWNFLAT_FOLDED_A == POISON_OWNFLAT_DECLARED,
       "poison_scene_own_flat: FIXTURE A folds to {POISON_OWNFLAT_FOLDED_A}, not the hand-derived {POISON_OWNFLAT_DECLARED} — a SAMPLED per-layer table must fold CAP_PER_LINE|CAP_DEFORM|CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE together, which is the positive form of the implication scene_caps() pins. If this moved, the refusal below is contrasting against the wrong thing")

// ---- FIXTURE B, THE POISON ----
ensure(POISON_OWNFLAT_FOLDED_B >= 0,
       "poison_scene_own_flat: unreachable — this ensure exists only to reference fixture B and force layer() to elaborate it")
